<div class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">HORIZON → INVOICEME</span><h1>Import your games</h1><p>A quick upload today. Less manual work for every invoice after.</p></div></div>
<div class="import-steps"><strong>01 Upload</strong><span>→</span><span>02 Match columns</span><span>→</span><span>03 Review & import</span></div>
<section class="card upload-card"><span class="empty-icon">↑</span><h2>Bring your Horizon export</h2><p>CSV or XLSX · up to 10 MB · up to 20,000 rows</p><%= form_with url: upload_games_path, multipart: true do |f| %><%= f.label :file, "Choose a master schedule or payroll export" %><%= f.file_field :file, accept: ".csv,.xlsx,.tsv", required: true %><%= f.submit "Continue to column matching →", class: "button primary" %><% end %></section>
<div class="two-cards"><section class="card"><h3>Use the whole season</h3><p>Set the date and game filters in Horizon before exporting. Include the game number, date, code, officials, and fees where available.</p><%= link_to "Download example CSV ↗", sample_games_path, class: "small-link" %></section><section class="card"><h3>Safe to import again</h3><p>Games are matched by game number within each year. Importing a newer export updates those games without adding duplicates. Other games remain in place.</p></section></div>
